<article class="env-lemma" id="01TV">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01TV">Lemma <span data-tag="01TV">29.22.7</span>.</a> A closed immersion $i : Z \to X$ is of finite presentation if and only if the associated quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals $\mathcal{I} = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(\mathcal{O}_ X \to i_*\mathcal{O}_ Z)$ is of finite type (as an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      On any affine open $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) \subset X$ we have $i^{-1}(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)) = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R/I)$ and $\mathcal{I} = \widetilde{I}$. Moreover, $\mathcal{I}$ is of finite type if and only if $I$ is a finite $R$-module for every such affine open (see Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/01PB" data-tag="01PB">28.17.1</a>). And $R/I$ is of finite presentation over $R$ if and only if $I$ is a finite $R$-module. Hence we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>